+---
+id: task-004-add-importtasks-bulk-import-helper
+type: task
+title: "Add importTasks bulk import helper"
+status: pending
+---
+
+## Request
+
+Add a public helper for bulk import, `importTasks(list, text)`, exported from `src/index.ts`. `text`
+holds one task per line as `title;priority;tags` (priority optionally blank for "normal", tags
+space-separated, blank lines skipped). It adds every valid line to `list` and returns
+`{ imported, rejected }`, with `rejected` as `{ line, reason }[]`, `line` counting from 1.
+
+## What was done
+
+- Added `src/import.ts`: `importTasks(list, text)`, plus the `ImportRejection` and `ImportResult`
+  types it returns. It splits `text` into lines, skips blank ones, parses each remaining line on its
+  first two semicolons (title / priority / tags), and hands the result to `list.add`. A line with
+  fewer than two semicolons is rejected before reaching `list.add`; every other rejection reason is
+  the list's own validation message (empty/too-long title, bad priority, bad tag, duplicate title).
+  See `dl-004` for the detailed rationale.
+- Exported `importTasks`, `ImportRejection` and `ImportResult` from `src/index.ts`.
+- Added `test/import.test.ts`: red-first tests (new behaviour) covering a title-only line, a line with
+  priority and multiple tags, blank-line handling (including line-number continuity after blanks), an
+  invalid-priority line, an empty-title line, a shapeless line, and a duplicate-title line.
+- `npm test` passes: 29/29 (22 pre-existing + 7 new).
+
+## Directive compliance
+
+- `r1-no-new-dependency`: no dependency added.
+- `r2-tsdoc-on-exports`: `importTasks`, `ImportRejection` and `ImportResult` all carry TSDoc.
+- `r3-no-clock-or-randomness`: not applicable (`src/import.ts` is outside `src/domain/`), and the file
+  reads neither anyway.
+- `r4-errors-as-result`: not applicable outside `src/domain/`; the function never throws and returns
+  the plain `{ imported, rejected }` shape the request specifies.
+- Testing directive: each acceptance criterion classified and tested red-first; happy-path and
+  error-path covered.
